# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored — NEVER commit real credentials.
# Loaded by scripts via lib/load-env.js (does not override vars already set in the real env).
#
# Auth for the headless Claude CLI that the onboarding learner (scripts/onboard-learn.js) spawns.
# Without credentials, a detached `claude -p` run reports "Not logged in" and the learn step fails.
# Pick ONE of the two options below.

# === Option A (preferred): reuse your Claude Code SUBSCRIPTION — no API key ===
# Generate a long-lived OAuth token from your subscription:
#     claude setup-token
# then paste it here. Works headlessly and is portable into Docker (inject via --env-file).
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# For LOCAL onboarding only, you can skip the token entirely if the CLI is already logged in
# (run `claude` once and /login). The spawned `claude -p` reuses that persisted login.
# A fresh Docker container has no such login, so use the token above for container runs.

# === Option B (alternative): API key ===
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com   # only if targeting a non-default endpoint

# === Optional ===
# Absolute path to the Claude CLI if it isn't on PATH (otherwise auto-resolved).
# Windows example (the desktop-app-bundled CLI):
# ZONOID_CLAUDE_BIN=C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Roaming\Claude\claude-code\<version>\claude.exe

# --- Docker (bench runs) ---
# Do NOT bake credentials into the image. Inject at run time, e.g.:
#   docker run --env-file .env.local ...
# or individually:  -e CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN   (or -e ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)
